; reg --group-by-cumulative carries the running total from one group into
; the next, as bal --group-by-cumulative carries account totals.  It used
; to abort (Assertion `last_post->has_xdata()'): the register's per-group
; flush cleared the journal's xdata between groups, while the chain kept
; pointing at the last posting of the previous group.  The --script block
; checks that the report still clears xdata when it ends, so the next
; command in the session starts from zero.  The --depth 1 and --dow
; blocks are characterization: those cumulative reports complete on the
; unfixed tree (their upstream filters emit only temporaries, which
; clear_xdata skips) and must print the same after the fix.

2012/01/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $50.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/03 Grocer
    Expenses:Food               $20.00
    Expenses:Utilities           $5.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/15 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          $55.00
    Assets:Checking

2012/02/20 Electric Company
    Expenses:Utilities          10 EUR
    Assets:Checking

test reg --group-by payee --group-by-cumulative Expenses
